{"team":"TEN","col":"#4FC3E8","identity":"run-heavy","funnel":"run-funnel","plays_pg":59.6,"adot":7.6,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>A Ground-First Machine</h2><p>The backfield runs through one man \u2014 <strong>Tony Pollard</strong> absorbs <strong>70% of the carries</strong> (league ~59%), a true bell-cow share that makes his rushing volume among the safest floors in the sport when the script cooperates.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>Few offenses are as committed to the run as TEN. Their pass rate over expected sits at <strong>-5%</strong> \u2014 well below the -2% norm \u2014 and it collapses to 38% once they're in front. The script writes itself: build a lead, then bludgeon.</p><p>When they fall behind they abandon the run entirely \u2014 62% pass while trailing, so their pass-catchers have huge comeback-script ceilings.</p><p>By the numbers it's a struggling unit \u2014 a 39% success rate (below the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Their red-zone identity is <strong>pass-first</strong> (54% pass), which puts scoring equity on <strong>Wan'Dale Robinson</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 Soft on the Ground</h2><p>They surrender <strong>125 rushing</strong> and <strong>219 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). The run moves against them \u2014 <strong>target opposing RB1s</strong>.</p><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR2s</strong> \u2014 44 rec yds/game (vs ~36). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They leak <strong>WR1 receiving TDs</strong> (0.53/game vs ~0.38) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>They lock down backs out of the backfield \u2014 just 13 rec yds/game (vs ~18); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They leak <strong>RB rushing TDs</strong> (0.53/game vs ~0.46) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: back <strong>Tony Pollard</strong>'s rushing volume in favored/positive scripts; their pass-catchers have massive ceilings in comeback scripts (fade-material as underdogs); <strong>opposing RB1s</strong> smash on the ground and at the goal line.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Cam Ward","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":11,"props":{"Comp":16.37,"Att":27.06,"Pass Yds":162.11,"Pass TD":0.79,"INT":0.35,"Rush Yds":11.58},"d":{"completions":16.37,"attempts":27.06,"pass_yards":162.11,"pass_td":0.79,"interceptions":0.35,"rush_att":2.51,"rush_yards":11.58}}],"RB":[{"name":"Tony Pollard","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":32,"props":{"Rush Att":21.3,"Rush Yds":95.0,"Tgt":3.03,"Rec":2.36,"Rec Yds":16.59},"d":{"rush_att":21.3,"rush_yards":95.0,"targets":3.03,"receptions":2.36,"rec_yards":16.59,"rec_td":0.04}},{"name":"Tyjae Spears","slot":"RB2","starter":true,"td":22,"props":{"Rush Att":5.54,"Rush Yds":22.52,"Tgt":4.7,"Rec":3.31,"Rec Yds":22.55},"d":{"rush_att":5.54,"rush_yards":22.52,"targets":4.7,"receptions":3.31,"rec_yards":22.55,"rec_td":0.06}},{"name":"Nicholas Singleton","slot":"RB3","starter":false,"td":15,"props":{"Rush Att":3.97,"Rush Yds":17.01,"Tgt":1.56,"Rec":1.04,"Rec Yds":7.48},"d":{"rush_att":3.97,"rush_yards":17.01,"targets":1.56,"receptions":1.04,"rec_yards":7.48,"rec_td":0.03}},{"name":"Julius Chestnut","slot":"RB4","starter":false,"td":8,"props":{"Rush Att":3.04,"Rush Yds":11.72,"Tgt":1.8,"Rec":1.19,"Rec Yds":9.54},"d":{"rush_att":3.04,"rush_yards":11.72,"targets":1.8,"receptions":1.19,"rec_yards":9.54,"rec_td":0.04}}],"WR":[{"name":"Carnell Tate","slot":"WR1","starter":true,"td":20,"props":{"Tgt":6.74,"Rec":4.33,"Rec Yds":54.01,"Rec TD":0.22},"d":{"targets":6.74,"receptions":4.33,"rec_yards":54.01,"rec_td":0.22}},{"name":"Wan'Dale Robinson","slot":"WR2","starter":true,"td":18,"props":{"Tgt":10.47,"Rec":7.23,"Rec Yds":67.63,"Rec TD":0.2},"d":{"targets":10.47,"receptions":7.23,"rec_yards":67.63,"rec_td":0.2}},{"name":"Calvin Ridley","slot":"WR3","starter":true,"td":14,"props":{"Tgt":5.24,"R